{"term":"invoice","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:faa4816ba08b758e17","definition":"A bill; a commercial document issued by a seller to a buyer indicating the products, quantities and agreed prices for products or services that the seller has already provided the buyer with. An invoice indicates that, unless paid in advance, payment is due by the buyer to the seller, according to the agreed terms.","example":"I've already rendered the invoices for payment.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["commercial invoice","e-invoice","invoice price"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invoice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:af0f477f449675806d","definition":"The lot or set of goods as shipped or received.","example":"The merchant receives a large invoice of goods.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["shipment"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["commercial invoice","e-invoice","invoice price"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invoice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ab49fa50643f54afd4","definition":"The price which a seller or dealer pays the manufacturer for goods to be sold.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["commercial invoice","e-invoice","invoice price"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/invoice#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:887c863239a8ec5389","definition":"A kind of receipt that serves as a tax document and sometimes also as a lottery ticket.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Taiwan","register":"Taiwan","wordFam